		<title type="html"><![CDATA[pinball with lorentz force]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=17000#p17000"><![CDATA[
Hi all,<br><br>please find attached an implementation of the lorentz force (F=q(E+v x B) ) in blender. There are two files in the zip:<br><br>lorentzdemo01.blend - use x,y and z to add velocity in the corresponding direction<br><br>lorentz pinball.blend - use space to plunge the charged ball, and alt and cmd to use the flippers. Magnetic field is in the same direction as gravity, leading to bend curves on the table.<br><br>One question: when running lorentzdemo01.blend the sphere disappears after a while. Any idea why?<br><br>Cheers,<br><br>arit<dl class="file"><dt><span class="imageset icon_topic_attach"></span> <a class="postlink" href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/download/file.php?id=412">lorentz pinball.zip</a></dt></dl><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=6196">arit</a> — Fri Jan 15, 2010 2:52 pm</p><hr />
